# build the image using docker compose

`docker-compose build`

# start the container

the `docker-compose.yml` uses user `1000:1000` by default, because poky doesn't like to be run by `root`.
adjust it to your needs and make sure the user has *rw* priviledges in `../poky`

`docker-compose up -d --remove-orphans`

# SQUEEZEOS_SRC_MIRROR
`SQUEEZEOS_SRC_MIRROR` is meant to be a generic url for all source packages, which are

- no longer available upstream
- complicated/impossible to download in an ancient linux distro (ssl problems)
- don't have a valid home

ideally those files are hosted by a squeezeos community - maybe later a default

configure `SQUEEZEOS_SRC_MIRROR` in either `docker-compose.yml` or in a renamed `poky/source-mirror.conf-example`

# enter the container

`docker exec -it docker-squeezeos-dev-1 bash`

# compile

`cd /poky`
`./set-source-mirror` # rolls out the `SQUEEZEOS_SRC_MIRROR` path defined above to multiple files and hardcodes BUILD_ARCH to i686, because docker host most likely ships x86_64

optionally `cp build/conf/local.conf.sample build/conf/local.conf` and adjust it to your needs
_(I only tested `MACHINE ?= "baby"`, so things might not work with other targets)_ 

`source poky-init-build-env`

`touch conf/sanity.conf` # required because we can't set `/proc/sys/vm/mmap_min_addr` in a container

# expand path, because else opkg-build is not found
`export PATH="$PATH:/poky/build/tmp-baby/work/i686-linux/opkg-utils-native-svn-r2/temp-staging/usr/local/bin/"` 


`bitbake squeezeos-image`


# bundled source files

## rootfs.tar.xz

the bundled `rootfs.tar.xz` is a copy from this repo:

https://github.com/yamamuteki/ubuntu-lucid-i386

you're welcome to contribute a more official archive.

## 20230114-updated-utilities-i386.tar.tgz

the bundled `20230114-updated-utilities-i386.tar.tgz` is a copy from

https://sourceforge.net/projects/lmsclients/files/squeezeos/

likely will be added to the global `SQUEEZEOS_SRC_MIRROR` of this repo

## sources.list

updated `sources.list` with available repo urls

